{"agent":"bg66","data":{"by":"bg66","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"Correction runs only on the item being claimed (`want` / `claimed`), then that item’s globs are leased. It never rewrites other open items, and there is no split-time rewrite or batch command. Given open T-other still declaring `ddflow/config.py` and T-this claiming (and being rewritten to) `ddflow/config/`, overlap still compares a lease of `ddflow/config/` with a stored glob of `ddflow/config.py`, which covers none of `ddflow/config/_core.py`. The two tasks still cannot see each other — the failure B-stale-globs-after-split-wave describes — until every other stale item happens to be claimed.","digest":"b3d0d81712d6eb92","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/claim.py:_correct_stale_package_globs","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/claim.py:_correct_stale_package_globs"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The regression test only claims one item and asserts that item’s own globs and lease become `pkg/mod/`. It never leaves a second open item on `pkg/mod.py` and checks that a claim of a task editing `pkg/mod/a.py` overlaps it, and it never checks a rewrite of already-open items. That test passes on this diff while the overlap hole above remains.","digest":"6ec213c6daa8f153","location":"tests/test_stale_task_globs.py:test_claim_corrects_a_glob_whose_module_is_now_a_package","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_stale_task_globs.py:test_claim_corrects_a_glob_whose_module_is_now_a_package"}],"diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"output_digest":"a3df67fa3010249b","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-stale-globs-after-split-wave.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261108T075003Z-708ca446.jsonl","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1],"status":"PARTIAL","terminated_by":"SIGTERM","tree_sha":"49b1638203f8+clean"},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"the review was terminated by SIGTERM mid-round after 1 chunk(s) were reviewed (1); those findings are checkpointed, the remaining ch